sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: One answer from the TTT chatbot
    accDescr: Flowbot calls start. The bot posts the question and graph ids to TTT and keeps elements with text. It builds the prompt, streams the language model's answer through onToken, and returns the text, the source documents and token counts. Empty results lead to a fixed fallback message.
    autonumber
    participant F as Flowbot /api/chat
    participant S as server/index.js
    participant T as TTT /v1/queries
    participant L as Language model
    F->>S: start(handler, question, onToken)
    S->>T: graph_ids, text, max_results 5 (Authorization from handler)
    T-->>S: elements
    S->>S: keep elements with non empty content
    S->>L: prompt with excerpts, temperature 0, stream
    loop tokens
        L-->>S: chunk
        S-->>F: onToken(chunk)
    end
    S-->>F: text, sourceDocuments, tokens
